# /etc/fw_env.config — U-Boot environment access configuration
# Used by fw_printenv / fw_setenv (libubootenv-tool package)
#
# Mono Gateway LS1046A: U-Boot env stored in SPI NOR flash (QSPI)
# DTS partition "uboot-env" = mtd2
#
# Format: Device   Offset   Env_size   Sector_size
# - Offset: 0x0 = start of the MTD partition (not flash absolute offset)
# - Env_size: 0x2000 (8 KB) — matches U-Boot CONFIG_ENV_SIZE
# - Sector_size: 0x1000 (4 KB) — QSPI NOR erase block from /proc/mtd
#
# WARNING: this offset has flip-flopped before and will again — it depends
# entirely on WHICH DTB is actually booted, not on anything in this repo's
# own numbering. Whichever DTB is primary changes how many partitions come
# before "uboot-env" in the DT, which shifts every mtd number after it.
# Before trusting this file, verify against a live `cat /proc/mtd`.
#
# Verified on live hardware 2026-04-03 (mono-gateway-dk.dts primary):
# /proc/mtd shows: mtd0=rcw-bl2, mtd1=uboot, mtd2=uboot-env, mtd3=fman-ucode
# brute-force test confirmed only 0x2000 produces valid CRC
# hexdump /dev/mtd2 shows CRC + ASCII key=value (arch=arm, bootcmd=...)
# 2026-07-01: some other "nxp-sdk DTB" then primary had uboot-env at mtd3:
# mtd2=uboot, mtd3=uboot-env, mtd4=fman-ucode, mtd5=recovery-dtb
# 2026-09-12: c92006b8 fixed DTB selection to build+use mono-gateway-dk-sdk.dts
# (which #includes mono-gateway-dk.dts, the same partition table as 04-03).
# `add system image` on real hardware confirmed fw_printenv fails against
# mtd3 (points at "fman-ucode") and /proc/mtd again reads mtd0=rcw-bl2,
# mtd1=uboot, mtd2=uboot-env, mtd3=fman-ucode -- back to mtd2, matching 04-03.
#
/dev/mtd2	0x0	0x2000	0x1000
